{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:50bf9823e62b1c3b","name":"Memory Upgrade","source":{"id":"source:reference-50bf9823e62b1c3b","title":"Memory Upgrade","revision":19709,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:28:02Z","sha256":"7ac5d996fc0ebf703cb4bef6fa12b4594d6a36db73ec97230aa7852312491d97","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19709","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Memory%20Upgrade&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-50bf9823e62b1c3b","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MEMORY UPGRADE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["UPGRADE POINT"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/UPGRADE_POINT"}," COST\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Standard\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["4,000\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Advanced\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["16,000\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Any device that has an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," score (such as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Portable Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Portable_Computer","referenceId":"reference:cab55f633363d43e"},") can have its Memory Upgraded, improving its performance and storage capacity. The Standard Memory Upgrade increases the device's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," by +2 and doubles the device's storage capacity. Unless otherwise specified, an unmodified computer holds a number of memory units equal to 5 x the square of the computer's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," bonus. (A single memory unit holds the same amount of data as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Recording Unit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Recording_Unit","referenceId":"reference:6d05309737113ae6"},", and 10 memory units are enough to hold coordinates for a single hyperspace jump.)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["An Advanced Memory Upgrade is also available, which increases ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," by +4 and multiplies the device's storage capacity by 5. (This replaces the the benefit of the Standard Memory Upgrade.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Memory Upgrade cannot be installed on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," (including ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droidified"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droidified"}," Equipment).\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
